oll has fielded in nearly three months against a challenger, Jennifer Jenkins, who carries Brevard name recognition.", "watch": "A fresh independent poll showing Jenkins closing within single digits, or a debate-driven shift on insurance and cost-of-living issues, would be the clearest sign the race is loosening.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 79 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Mike Haridopolos (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican Rep. Mike Haridopolos seeks re-election in this Space Coast district, which leans Republican by about eight points. Democrat Jennifer Jenkins, a former Brevard County school board member, has run a funded campaign, but she trails in money: Haridopolos has raised roughly $1.8 million to her $914,000 and holds a wide cash advantage heading into the final stretch.\n\nPolling has been sparse, with just two July surveys, one Republican-sponsored and one Democratic-sponsored, each showing Haridopolos ahead by nine points. Rating organizations across the spectrum place the race between Likely and Safe Republican, and prediction markets give Democrats little chance. Jenkins's strongest arguments center on insurance costs and affordability, themes that surfaced repeatedly in their debates. Haridopolos's endorsements, including the U.S. Chamber, and local funding announcements reinforce his incumbent position. The expected margin is about ten points for the incumbent.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0724, "margin": -8.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0723, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0928, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0611, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0442, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0553, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0651, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0689, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0604, "margin": -10.5}, {